    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3). The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and its three postcode scenarios \u2014 store valid, accept absent, reject malformed \u2014 all pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, region-validated `postcode` on owner creation. Postcode is validated **only when present** and stays optional when absent, so the request contract is backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `postcode` (optional string, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `OwnerFields` feeds both the request DTO and the `Owner` response schema, the generated DTOs get a `postcode` field (validated/returned), and the `@Pattern` constraint rejects a non-4-digit value with 400 via bean validation.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions (no mapper change needed).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `validatePostcode(city, postcode)`, called during `addOwner`. When a postcode is present it must be 4 digits and, if the city maps to a known region (`LocalityLookup`: NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), fall within that range; an out-of-range value throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. Absent/blank postcode returns early (accepted).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column to `hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, and `postgres` `schema.sql` (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`), and added the corresponding `NULL` value to the hsqldb `data.sql` positional owner inserts (the other DBs use explicit column lists and were unaffected).\n\nNote: the region-range check runs on the create path (`POST /api/owners`), which is what the spec and tests exercise; `updateOwner` was left untouched as it doesn't handle postcode.",
